<title>SPAIN: Spanish bond market closed for public holiday.</title>
<headline>Spanish bond market closed for public holiday.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1997-07-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Spain's government bond market was closed on Friday for a local holiday in Madrid. Trade will resume as normal on Monday.</p>
<p>Closing levels for bonds on Thursday were as follows: * 10-yr 7.35 pct T-bond 108.44 vs 108.75, yield 6.15 vs 6.11 * Sept bond future 117.99 vs 118.23 at Wednesday's close. * Peseta/mark 84.25/27 vs 84.21/22.</p>
<p>-- Madrid newsroom + 34 1 585 2161</p>
